  "final_text": "The dashboard and the alert rule both exist, and the rule is enabled. I read both back from Kibana to confirm. The rule has already run once and reported status `ok`, so the query executes without errors.\n\n**1. The data.** The `Kibana Sample Data Logs` data view (index `kibana_sample_data_logs`) has one document per web request. Its time field is `timestamp`. The main fields are:\n- `response` / `response.keyword`: the HTTP status code, stored as text\n- `bytes`: size of the response\n- `clientip`: the visitor's IP address\n- `url`, `request`, `extension`: what was requested\n- `geo.src`, `geo.dest`, `geo.coordinates`: where traffic came from and went\n- `agent`, `machine.os`: the visitor's browser and operating system\n- `referer`, `tags`, `host`\n\n**2. Dashboard \"EFF-76e7c93e Web logs overview\"** has 8 panels and defaults to the last 7 days: http://localhost:15601/app/dashboards#/view/eff-76e7c93e-web-logs-overview-c561c2f35624\n- **Headline numbers:** total requests, unique visitors (distinct client IPs) and total bytes served.\n- **Requests over time:** a line chart.\n- **Response codes over time:** a stacked bar chart split by status code.\n- **Response code share:** a pie chart.\n- **Top requested URLs:** a table with request count and bytes.\n- **Top source countries:** a bar chart.\n\n**3. Rule \"EFF-76e7c93e 5xx spike\"** (id `6e72fad1-9182-4921-a2c4-25312b6a316f`) is an Elasticsearch query rule:\n- It runs every minute.\n- Each run counts requests in the last 5 minutes whose status code starts with \"5\".\n- It fires when that count is more than 10.\n\n**Limitations:**\n- **No notifications:** the rule has no actions attached. It records alerts in Kibana but doesn't notify anyone. Add a connector (Slack, email, etc.) if you want messages.\n- **Empty API key:** `KIBANA_TEST_API_KEY` was empty in this environment, so I couldn't query Elasticsearch directly. I built everything through the Kibana MCP tools and didn't check the actual status-code values in the data. The 5xx filter assumes the usual sample-data values (200, 404, 503).",
